// №362 (p362-advice, p-bignum-tuple Defect A, Problem 1+2): E_READONLY_COERCE's
// suggestion (b) is `@field.clone()` — but `Clone` is opt-in (D230, `#impl
// (Clone)`), so it only actually exists when the FIELD's type opted in.
// Applying the advice literally on a field type that did NOT (a plain
// named tuple, no `#impl(Clone)`) must fail HONESTLY at check-time with
// `E7320` (no such method) — NOT silently pass `nova check` and corrupt
// codegen downstream with a misresolved receiver (`E_RECV_METHOD_MISMATCH`,
// the original — worse — symptom nova-bignum hit,
// docs/plans/wip/PROGRESS-p-bignum-tuple.md).
//
// Root cause (found this window): `infer_expr_type`'s `Member` arm
// (compiler-codegen/src/types/mod.rs) had NO `TypeDeclKind::NamedTuple` case
// — only `Record`. So `infer_expr_type(@field, scope)` returned `None`
// whenever the ENCLOSING type of `@field` (here, `Self` — `P362MDec`) was
// itself a named tuple, independent of the field's own type. That silent
// `None` short-circuits `f3_check_member_ctx` (~15042: `let Some(obj_tr) =
// self.infer_expr_type(obj, scope) else { return; }`) — the function that
// exists specifically to validate a CHAINED member/method access — so
// `@mant.clone()` (or `@mant.anything`) type-checked with ZERO diagnostics.
// Fixed by adding the missing `NamedTuple` arm, mirroring the existing
// `Record` one (same field-lookup + generic-substitution shape).
//
// EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR E7320

module neg.p362_clone_advice_no_impl_neg

import std.collections.vec.{Vec}

// No `#impl(Clone)` — this named tuple never opted into `Clone` (D230).
type P362MInt(sign int, limbs Vec[u32])

type P362MDec(mant P362MInt, scale int)

fn P362MDec.new(mant P362MInt, scale int) -> P362MDec => P362MDec(mant, scale)

// RO-receiver method: `@mant` is not fully-stack (heap `Vec[u32]` field) so
// a bare `mut mant = @mant` would trip `E_READONLY_COERCE`, whose own
// suggestion (b) is exactly the `.clone()` below.
fn P362MDec @normalize() -> P362MInt {
    mut mant = @mant.clone()
    mant
}

fn main() -> () {
    ro d = P362MDec.new(P362MInt(1, Vec[u32].of(1, 2, 3)), 0)
    print(d.normalize().sign)
}
